course: dictionary
lesson: 8804
title: A festival word in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have met before, such as a festival. Context helps: read the words around the word and ask what it could be. «The first Pentecost happened during a Jewish harvest feast, Shavuot, held fifty days after Passover.» The clues are harvest feast and after Passover, so Shavuot must be a feast linked to harvest time.
explain: The commas are a clue too. In «a Jewish harvest feast, Shavuot,» the comma sets the name apart, so Shavuot is another name for that feast. When a word is followed by a comma and then explained, the explanation tells you what it means.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Shavuot is a festival, so «Jewish families celebrate Shavuot» still makes sense. When context is not enough, a dictionary or a teacher will tell you the full story.
fact: Shavuot is a Jewish festival that comes seven weeks after Passover.
fact: Shavuot celebrates the giving of the Torah to Moses on Mount Sinai.
fact: Shavuot also celebrates the wheat harvest, so it is a harvest feast too.
fact: Shavuot is also called the Feast of Weeks.
fact: Jewish families decorate their homes with flowers and greenery, read the Book of Ruth and eat dairy foods like cheesecake.
exercise: «The first Pentecost happened during a Jewish harvest feast, Shavuot, held fifty days after Passover.» What is Shavuot? | A Jewish name for the wheat harvest | *A Jewish festival, also called the Feast of Weeks | A kind of greenery | A type of cheesecake
exercise: What does Shavuot celebrate? | The end of winter | The building of a new village | Noah's ark and the first snow | *The giving of the Torah to Moses and the wheat harvest
exercise: Find and copy the word that links Shavuot to the harvest. | *harvest | Passover | Pentecost | fifty
test: Shavuot comes seven weeks after which festival? | Christmas | Diwali | *Passover | Hanukkah
test: Which book do Jewish families read during Shavuot? | The Book of Psalms | The Book of Genesis | *The Book of Ruth
exam: What is the best way to work out what Shavuot means in a sentence? | Guess the first letter and stop | Ask for the spelling only | *Read the words around it, then swap your meaning in and check it still fits | Skip the word and never think about it again
